  "description": "The fMRIPrep run was launched for subject **sub\u201101**, session **ses\u201101**, targeting the resting\u2011state task (task\u2011id\u202f=\u202f\u201crest\u201d) and using echo\u202f1 (echo\u2011idx\u202f=\u202f\u201c1\u201d). A unique run identifier of\u202f123e4567\u2011e89b\u201112d3\u2011a456\u2011426614174000 was assigned. The preprocessing included two dummy scans (dummy\u2011scans\u202f=\u202f2) and employed ICA\u2011AROMA (use\u2011aroma\u202f=\u202ftrue) with the default melodic dimensionality of\u202f\u2011200. No files were excluded from processing (ignore\u202f=\u202f\u201c\u201d), and BIDS validation was performed (skip\u2011bids\u2011validation\u202f=\u202ffalse, gear\u2011run\u2011bids\u2011validation\u202f=\u202ftrue). Verbosity was set to \u201cvv\u201d, and the pipeline was configured to write no boiler\u2011plate text (boilerplate\u202f=\u202ffalse, md\u2011only\u2011boilerplate\u202f=\u202ffalse). All standard preprocessing steps were run (anat\u2011only\u202f=\u202ffalse, longitudinal\u202f=\u202ffalse, t2s\u2011coreg\u202f=\u202ffalse), and the output space was limited to the MNI152NLin2009cAsym template. Coregistration of BOLD to T1w used six degrees of freedom (bold2t1w\u2011dof\u202f=\u202f6), with neither forced nor prohibited BBR (force\u2011bbr\u202f=\u202ffalse, force\u2011no\u2011bbr\u202f=\u202ffalse). The skull\u2011stripping used the OASIS30ANTs template (skull\u2011strip\u2011template\u202f=\u202f\u201cOASIS30ANTs\u201d) without a fixed random seed, and no spline interpolation or de\u2011meaning was applied to field maps (fmap\u2011bspline\u202f=\u202ffalse, fmap\u2011no\u2011demean\u202f=\u202ffalse). Surface reconstruction proceeded with the standard FreeSurfer workflow (fs\u2011no\u2011reconall\u202f=\u202ffalse, gear\u2011keep\u2011fsaverage\u202f=\u202ffalse) using the FreeSurfer license file named\u202flicense.txt (gear\u2011FREESURFER_LICENSE\u202f=\u202f\u201clicense.txt\u201d, freesurfer_license\u202fpath\u202f=\u202f\u201c/opt/freesurfer/license.txt\u201d). No additional CIFTI output, sub\u2011millimetre reconstruction, or resource monitoring was requested, and the run was not set to stop on the first crash (stop\u2011on\u2011first\u2011crash\u202f=\u202ffalse).\n\nThe computational resources allocated for this job were eight CPU cores (n_cpus\u202f=\u202f8) and 16\u202fGB of RAM (mem_mb\u202f=\u202f16000). Motion\u2011scrubbing thresholds were the defaults (framewise\u2011displacement\u202f=\u202f0.5\u202fmm, DVARS\u202f=\u202f1.5), and the pipeline was instructed not to write any execution graph, intermediate files, or intermediate folders (write\u2011graph\u202f=\u202ffalse, gear\u2011save\u2011intermediate\u2011output\u202f=\u202ffalse, gear\u2011intermediate\u2011files\u202f=\u202f\u201c\u201d, gear\u2011intermediate\u2011folders\u202f=\u202f\u201c\u201d). Logging was kept at the INFO level (gear\u2011log\u2011level\u202f=\u202f\u201cINFO\u201d), and all optional tracking was disabled (notrack\u202f=\u202ffalse, gear\u2011abort\u2011on\u2011bids\u2011error\u202f=\u202ffalse). The run was executed as a dry run? No \u2013 the dry\u2011run flag was off (gear\u2011dry\u2011run\u202f=\u202ffalse), and none of the output preservation options were enabled (gear\u2011keep\u2011output\u202f=\u202ffalse). In summary, the configuration reflects a standard fMRIPrep execution with ICA\u2011AROMA enabled, default quality\u2011control thresholds, and full BIDS compliance for the specified resting\u2011state dataset."
